1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,704
Ever wonder why you can feel okay right

2
00:00:05,724 --> 00:00:08,207
after a concussion… and then feel terrible

3
00:00:08,227 --> 00:00:08,565
later?

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,816
That's because a concussion doesn't always

5
00:00:11,836 --> 00:00:13,733
cause something you can see from the

6
00:00:13,753 --> 00:00:14,159
outside.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,579
After an injury, the brain can temporarily

8
00:00:20,599 --> 00:00:23,178
have trouble communicating efficiently and

9
00:00:23,198 --> 00:00:25,653
managing the energy it needs to function

10
00:00:25,673 --> 00:00:26,210
normally.

11
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,708
That can affect everything from

12
00:00:31,728 --> 00:00:33,947
concentration and memory to balance,

13
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:36,434
energy, and how you process information.

14
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,509
And symptoms can fluctuate.

15
00:00:41,529 --> 00:00:43,660
You might feel pretty good one day and

16
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,679
struggle the next.

17
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,685
Sometimes, too much physical or mental

18
00:00:53,705 --> 00:00:55,989
activity can temporarily make symptoms

19
00:00:56,009 --> 00:00:58,173
worse. That doesn't necessarily mean

20
00:00:58,193 --> 00:01:00,114
you're getting new brain damage—

21
00:01:00,134 --> 00:01:02,661
it can mean your brain needs a little more

22
00:01:02,681 --> 00:01:04,905
time and the right recovery strategy.

23
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,592
If your symptoms are sticking around,

24
00:01:09,612 --> 00:01:11,168
don't just push through them.

25
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:13,452
Get evaluated and find out what your brain

26
00:01:13,472 --> 00:01:13,778
needs.

